Storage (Amazon S3): The mobile application requests a secure, temporary link and uploads the raw .mp4 file directly to a cloud bucket.
The Catalyst (AWS Lambda): The exact millisecond the upload finishes, 
an S3 event automatically wakes up a lightweight background function (Lambda). 
This function reads the file's name and location.
The Heavy Lifter (AWS Elemental MediaConvert): The Lambda function doesn't process the video itself. 
It instantly hands a "processing job ticket" to MediaConvert. MediaConvert spins up dedicated virtual processing units,
chops the video into 6-second adaptive bitrate streaming slices (.m3u8 playlist and .ts files),
and saves them into a separate public folder for stutter-free playback in India
